<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Ch. XIII — bovid horns as logarithmic spirals wound on a cone (Pass 1) — Code-to-model traceability: 70/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring maps E1-E5 to Thompson's pages; each model function cites its equation id; reference.json carries the thompson_locus for each equation; the Lean file cites pages and equation ids. Deductions: the figure-digitisation steps (sector choice, farthest-point rule) are documented in reference.json but not tied to any Thompson procedure (he measured whorl breadth ratios, Ch. XI p. 558), and verdict thresholds are asserted in reference.json without derivation." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Ch. XIII — bovid horns as logarithmic spirals wound on a cone (Pass 1) — Model fidelity to source: 62/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "E1-E3 are implemented exactly as Thompson states them (k = sin(beta) cot(alpha), R = e^(2 pi sin beta cot alpha), p. 558) and the gnomonic tube (E4) is rendered; the Lean module proves the whorl-ratio invariance, breadth law, projection non-identifiability and growth-velocity lemmas with 0 sorry. Deductions: the fit is done to a 2D projection with beta = 90 deg assumed when converting k to alpha, so the quantity compared to Thompson's 75 deg is alpha_proj, not alpha; E4 (breadth shares k) is formalised but not measured; E5 (velocity ratio) is only a rendering, not a fitted quantity." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-031_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks-with-a.py L444–L473: verdict_from compares alpha_proj (beta = 90 assumed) directly with Thompson's 75 deg <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/b0060c02/thompson/claims/t1917-031_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks-with-a.py#L444-L473>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 6.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Ch. XIII — bovid horns as logarithmic spirals wound on a cone (Pass 1) — Morphometric validation: 48/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Quantitative: alpha_proj, R, Pearson r, RMSE and two delta-AIC values are computed on the digitised figure and compared with Thompson's published 75 deg and with explicit null models; measure_morphoeval returns 6 rows with reference values. Missing: no uncertainty (bootstrap CI, KS test), no breadth / inner-edge gnomonic test (E4), n = 1 drawing, no real specimen, and the registry Dryad table is pinned but not even summarised." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
