<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-031-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Ch. XIII — bovid horns as logarithmic spirals wound on a cone (Pass 1) — Morphological realism / specimen match: 35/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The rendered comparison overlays the fitted spiral on Thompson's own figure and the overlay follows the dorsal and posterior edge closely, but (i) no real specimen is used in Pass 1 — the CC BY-SA Argali photograph is vendored and pinned but not analysed; (ii) the ventral end of the digitised edge includes the mandible junction (ln rho rises at the last 15 deg); (iii) the 3D helicoid panel uses beta = 60 deg chosen by hand, not fitted; (iv) only one species is shown, so the \"distinct morphologies distinct\" test is not exercised." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
